{{if .Monorepo}}## Monorepo

No `go.mod` or `.gitignore` were generated here — this service shares the
one at `{{.RootDirDisplay}}` with the rest of the monorepo. Two things
that are on you to wire up, since this tool won't edit files it didn't
create:

- Add `/{{.ServiceName}}` to the root `.gitignore` (the build output of
  `go build ./{{.RelDir}}`, same as every other service's binary there).
- Add this service to however the monorepo already builds/deploys the
  others — the generated `Dockerfile` builds correctly from the repo
  root (`docker build -f {{.RelDir}}/Dockerfile -t {{.ServiceName}} .`),
  but nothing wires that into an existing CI pipeline automatically.

